WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.968
Before naming a lower-origin rhythm, decide whether it is late and protective or early and ectopic. A junctional escape may prevent a prolonged pause after sinus failure. A premature ventricular beat instead interrupts the expected schedule. The origin alone does not explain the beat’s role.
命名较低起源节律前，应判断它是迟到的保护性激动，还是提前的异位搏动。窦性失效后的交界性逸搏可能避免长停顿，室性早搏则打断预期节奏；仅说起源并不能解释作用。

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:37.608
Use the backup hierarchy as a reference, then assess the actual patient. An escape rate may be inadequate for one patient but temporarily tolerated by another. Treating a protective rhythm as something to suppress can remove the remaining source of ventricular activation.
可用备用层级作参考，但须评估实际患者。同样逸搏频率可能对某人不足、对另一人暂时可耐受。若把保护性节律当成应抑制对象，可能除去剩余的心室激动来源。

00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:57.816
An AV-junctional impulse may activate the atria backwards. A retrograde P may therefore be inverted before QRS, hidden within it or seen afterwards. The QRS is often narrow because the normal ventricular conduction system is still used, unless another conduction abnormality is present.
房室交界区激动可逆向激动心房，因此逆行 P 波可能倒置于 QRS 前、藏在其中，或出现在其后。若仍使用正常心室传导系统，QRS 常较窄；合并其他传导异常时则不一定。

00:00:57.816 --> 00:01:17.688
The school calls forty to sixty an escape rhythm, sixty to one hundred accelerated junctional rhythm, and above one hundred junctional tachycardia. Consider sinus suppression, vagal effects, ischemia, digoxin exposure or postoperative context, and assess whether perfusion is sufficient.
学校把40至60称交界性逸搏，60至100称加速性交界性节律，超过100称交界性心动过速。应考虑窦性抑制、迷走作用、缺血、地高辛暴露或术后背景，并评估灌注是否足够。

00:01:17.688 --> 00:01:38.352
A PVC is an early ventricular complex, typically wide and unusual in shape, without an associated conducted P beforehand. A compensatory pause may follow, but not every PVC has the textbook pause. Describe what is present rather than forcing every feature into a fixed template.
室早是提前出现的心室波群，常较宽、形态异常，前面没有相关下传 P 波。随后可能有代偿间歇，但并非每个室早都符合教科书间歇。应描述所见，不要强迫每项特征都符合模板。

00:01:38.352 --> 00:02:01.320
Unifocal PVCs share a shape; multifocal ectopy has differing shapes. Bigeminy alternates an ectopic beat with another beat, and couplets are two consecutive PVCs. A beat falling during vulnerable repolarization raises concern. Check the patient and reversible causes instead of treating the pattern in isolation.
单源室早形态相似，多源异位活动有不同形态。二联律为异位搏动与另一搏动交替，成对室早是连续两个室早。落在易损复极期的搏动值得警惕；应检查患者和可逆原因，而不是孤立处理图形。

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:21.816
Monomorphic VT shows a rapid sequence of broadly similar ventricular complexes. The school gives a typical range of one hundred fifty to two hundred fifty, but slower ventricular tachycardias exist. A dangerous wide-complex rhythm cannot be dismissed because it falls outside a memorized range.
单形室速表现为快速、形态相近的心室波群序列。学校给出常见范围150至250次/分，但也存在较慢室速。不能因为宽波群危险节律不落在背诵范围内就将其排除。

00:02:21.816 --> 00:02:43.920
Assess responsiveness, breathing and pulse promptly. Pulseless VT follows the cardiac-arrest pathway. A pulse-present wide-complex tachycardia requires urgent stability assessment and authorized expertise; recognizing it does not authorize a PCP to select cardioversion or antiarrhythmic medication independently.
应迅速评估反应、呼吸与脉搏。无脉室速进入心搏骤停流程；有脉宽波群心动过速需要紧急稳定性评估和授权专家支持。识别出来不意味着 PCP 可独立选择电复律或抗心律失常药。

00:02:43.920 --> 00:03:03.048
Ventricular fibrillation is disorganized ventricular activity without useful coordinated beats. In true sustained VF, the patient has no effective pulse. If someone is alert with a reproducible pulse while a lead looks chaotic, investigate artifact without abandoning assessment.
室颤是缺乏有效协调搏动的无组织心室活动。真正持续室颤时，患者没有有效脉搏；若患者清醒且有可重复确认的脉搏，但某导联杂乱，应调查伪差，同时继续评估。

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:21.912
For an unresponsive pulseless patient, promptly follow the applicable resuscitation and defibrillation protocol. Technical confirmation and checks of the leads must not become a prolonged interruption of CPR. The patient’s condition and the shockable pattern guide action together.
对无反应、无脉患者，应迅速遵循适用的复苏与除颤流程。技术确认和导联核对不能演变为长时间中断 CPR；患者状态与可除颤形态共同指导行动。

00:03:21.912 --> 00:03:41.712
An idioventricular escape rhythm is a slow ventricular backup, generally without preceding conducted P waves and with a wide QRS. The school uses twenty to forty per minute as a reference. It may indicate profound failure of higher pacing or conduction and inadequate cardiac output.
室性逸搏节律是较慢的心室备用节律，通常无前置下传 P 波，QRS 较宽。学校以每分钟20至40次为参考，可能提示上级起搏或传导严重失败、心输出量不足。

00:03:41.712 --> 00:04:01.248
Accelerated idioventricular rhythm is the same ventricular-origin pattern at a faster rate, about forty to one hundred in this teaching. It can occur around reperfusion and may be tolerated. Do not suppress it merely to obtain a sinus-looking monitor; assess the underlying cause and circulation.
加速性室性自主节律是在本课约40至100次/分的较快心室起源形态，可见于再灌注前后，有时可耐受。不能仅为了让监护看起来像窦律就抑制它，应评估原因与循环。

00:04:01.248 --> 00:04:20.880
Before accepting a flat line as asystole, verify electrode and cable contact, suitable gain and another lead when feasible. A disconnected cable or fine VF can mislead. Do these checks within the resuscitation workflow, not instead of treating a patient without circulation.
接受平线为心静止前，应在可行时核对电极、线缆、合适增益及其他导联；脱线或细颤可能误导。这些检查应融入复苏流程，不能代替对无循环患者的处置。

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:40.608
Organized electrical activity without a pulse is a different branch, pulseless electrical activity. It is not proof of circulation and is not made shockable simply by having visible complexes. Follow the applicable arrest pathway and assess causes without prolonged diagnostic delays.
有组织电活动但无脉属于另一个分支——无脉性电活动。可见波群不能证明循环，也不会因此自动成为可除颤节律。应遵循适用骤停流程并评估原因，避免长时间诊断延误。

00:04:40.608 --> 00:04:59.184
The school cause groups include oxygenation problems, electrolyte disturbance, ischemia, structural disease and medication effects. Use them to direct questions and assessment, not to diagnose a potassium value from an isolated wave. Treatable causes may coexist.
学校列出的原因包括氧合问题、电解质异常、缺血、结构性疾病及药物效应。可据此组织问诊和检查，但不能从孤立波形诊断血钾值；多个可处理原因也可能并存。

00:04:59.184 --> 00:05:15.888
Communicate a useful sentence: a suspected ventricular-origin pattern at an estimated rate, with or without a pulse, plus the patient’s signs of perfusion and deterioration. That report is more actionable than a rhythm name detached from the patient.
报告应形成有用的一句话：疑似心室起源形态、估计心率、有脉或无脉，加上灌注和恶化表现。这样的信息比脱离患者的节律名称更可用于行动。
